  "raw_text": "149\n\nLaki maikaia\n \n(v) (Note that\n \nMaikaia\n \nis the “\nyou-object\n” form of the verb\n \nYabaia\n \n/ Tenga en cuenta que\n \nMaikaia\n\nes la forma de \"usted-objeto\" del verbo\n \nYabaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto pass on to you, to transmit to you, to transfer to you\n \n/\npasar a usted, transmitirle, transferirle\n\nMail\n \n(\ndb,sgd\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmile\n \n/ milla\n\nMain\n \n(a/t:\n \nMaind\n-\ndict\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncare\n \n/ cuidado\n\n(Note/Nota: From the English word:\n \nmind\n \n/ De la palabra inglesa:\n \nmind\n)\n \nConfirm that this word is used on its own\n\nMain kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto mind, to take care of, to watch, to guard\n \n/ cuidar, mirar, proteger\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/18\n):\n \nAlmuk nani ba spirit lainka ra sîp nani ra plun dakakisa, kaina kahbisa bara main kaikisa.\n \n–\n \nElders\nfeed the sheep spiritually, protect, and care for (them).\n \n/ Los ancianos alimentan a las ovejas espiritualmente, las\nprotegen y las cuidan.)\n\nMain ai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto mind me, to take care of me, to watch me, to guard me\n \n/ cuidarme, mirarme,\nprotegerme\n\nMain kaikaia warkka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwork to take care of someone or something,\n \nmaintenance work\n \n(\njl16\n) /\ntrabajo de cuidar a alguien o algo, trabajo de mantenimiento (\njl16\n)\n\nWatla ba main kaikaia warkka\n \n–\n \nbuilding maintenance work\n \n/ trabajo de mantenimiento de\nedificios\n\nMain kaikras kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto neglect, to not care for, to not protect\n \n/ descuidar, no cuidar, no proteger\n\nMain kakaira\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nwatcher, guard\n \n/ vigilante, guardia\n\n(Construct:\n \nMain kakairika\n)\n\nSîp main kakaira\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nshepherd\n \n/ pastor\n \n(Alt:\n \nSepad\n)\n\nMain mai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto mind you, to take care of you, to watch you, to guard you\n \n/ cuidarte, protegerte\n\nMaîra\n \n(\ndictu,lv\n)\n \n–\n \nmarried\n \n/ casado, casada\n \ncommonly used?\n\nMâira\n \n(\ndictu,db-Smasmalkra 2:5\n)\n \n–\n \nfruitful\n \n/ fructífero\n\nÂuya mâira\n \n(a/t:\n \nÂuya mâkira\n,\n \nAuyamakira\n,\n \nÂuyamakira\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nshrewd, intelligent, cautious, crafty, having a\ngood memory\n \n/ astuto, inteligente, cauteloso, de buena memoria\n\nÂuya mâira lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nshrewdness, intelligence\n \n/ astucia, inteligencia\n\nMairikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto show me\n \n/ mostrarme\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nMarikaia\n \n–\n \nto show\n \n/ mostrar;\n \nMamrikaia\n \n–\n \nto show\nyou\n \n/ mostrarte)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nWitin ai utla warkka ba mairikan\n \n–\n \nHe showed me his homework\n \n/ Me mostró su tarea)\n\nMairin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwoman, female\n \n/ mujer, hembra\n\n(Construct:\n \nMairka\n)\n\nWaitna mairin wal yapaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsex\n \n/ sexo\n\nMairin\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nwoman, female\n \n/ mujer, hembra\n\nLuhpa mairin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndaughter\n \n/ hija\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy92\n):\n \nLuhpi mairin ba siknis pali sa\n \n–\n \nMy daughter is very sick\n \n/ Mi hija esta muy enferma)\n\nMairin tiara\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nyoung girl\n \n/ jovencita\n\nMarit mairin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwife\n \n/\n \nesposa\n\n(Construct:\n \nMaritki mairin\n \n–\n \nmy wife\n \n/ mi esposa;\n \nMaritkam mairin\n \n–\n \nyour wife\n \n/ su esposa;\n \nMaritka mairin\n \n–\n \nhis wife\n \n/ su\nesposa)\n\nMaya mairin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwife\n \n/ esposa\n\nTuktan mairin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngirl\n \n/ niña\n\nMaisa\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nMaihsa\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwaist\n \n/ cintura\n\n(Construct:\n \nMaisi\n \n–\n \nmy waist\n \n/ mi cintura;\n \nMaisam\n \n–\n \nyour waist\n \n/ tu cintura;\n \nAi maisa\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their waist\n \n/ su cintura)\n\nMaisa\n \nkapaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nMaisakapaia\n,\n \nMaisha kapaia\n,\n \nMaihsa kapaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto instigate, to incite, to challenge, to provoke\n \n/\ninstigar, incitar, desafiar, provocar\n\nMaisa\n \nkapanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nMaisakapanka\n-\nbh31\n,\n \nMaisha kapanka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nchallenge, incitement, provocation,\ninstigation\n \n/ desafío, incitación, provocación, instigación\n\nMaisa\n \nnihkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nMaisanihkaia\n-\nmy,bh,\n \nMaisha nihkaia\n,\n \nMaihsa nihkaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto comfort\n \n/ consolar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-01/20\n):\n \nNahki tnatka ra Jehova mita Pal ra maisa nihkan ki?\n \n–\n \nIn what way was Paul comforted by Jehovah?\n \n/ ¿De qué\nmanera fue consolado Pablo por Jehová?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlff\n-\n29\n-\n2\n):\n \nPrura dukiara Baibil d\nî\na smalki ba wan maisa nihkisa.\n \n–\n \nWhat the Bible says about death comforts us.\n \n/\n \nL\no que dice\n\nla Biblia acerca de la muerte\n \nnos consuela\n.\n)",
